Z||000004||Primaris||08-28-2001||05:15 AM||||Yea in the fuse box.  The fuse box is down by your left foot under the dash.  There are two levers that you squeeze towards each other.  Then the whole fuse box will lower towards the back of the car.  Or you can lie down on the floor at stare up at it.  The fuse is (with panel lowerd) located in the upper left corner.  <P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||08-28-2001||09:47 AM||||Does your Check Engine light come on when you turn the key "on" (engine not running)?  Can you hear the fuel pump run for a couple of seconds as soon as you turn the key "on"?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroburton||08-28-2001||12:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Does your Check Engine light come on when you turn the key "on" (engine not running)?  Can you hear the fuel pump run for a couple of seconds as soon as you turn the key "on"?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the check engine light does not come on and i cant hear a hum like before and the fuses are all good , i cant get any codes from it ether  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||baptistheart||08-28-2001||12:36 PM||||Check your ecm (i believe thats what it's called) it's a little black rectangle shaped thing near your carb if you have a four.<BR>Not sure where it is on sixes.<BR>they have a habit of just going out and leaving you stranded. their pretty inexpensive to replace<P>Just noticed the computer is called the ecm so i'll call it the little black rectangular dohickey<BR>------------------<BR>Joe<p>[This message has been edited by baptistheart (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroburton||08-28-2001||01:00 PM||||here is a pic were is it located ?<BR>on the right or left ? thnx for your help<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/21_21.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Indiana_resto_guy||08-28-2001||01:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baptistheart:<BR><B>Check your ecm (i believe thats what it's called) it's a little black rectangle shaped thing near your carb if you have a four.<BR>Not sure where it is on sixes.<BR>they have a habit of just going out and leaving you stranded. their pretty inexpensive to replace<P>Just noticed the computer is called the ecm so i'll call it the little black rectangular dohickey</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Defination of: little black rectangular dohickey;<BR>MAS, short for Mass Air flow Sensor, location(s) 4 cylinder mounted on air cleaner, 6 cylinder mounted on left side near center of upper plenum.<P>Check your fuse links located at junction block on the passenger side to the rear of the battery. One of these supply voltage to the ECM (Electronic Control Module)it may have blown.<P>When you turn on the key, what lights light up on the instrument(s)?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fldevel||08-28-2001||02:35 PM||||just happen to me .. replaced ignition modual .. still dident start .. so i bought a new cap and rotor for like $15 and it started right up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">..but my guess would be ignition someware ||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||08-28-2001||02:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroburton:<BR><B> the check engine light does not come on and i cant hear a hum like before and the fuses are all good , i cant get any codes from it ether   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This sounds like you are not getting power to the ECM (or it's not grounded). Does everything else electrical work; lights, radio, turn signals, heater, etc...? <P>What year/engine/tranny is this?<P>If the fuses are good it's probably a loose connection or possibly a blown fuseable link. Do you have a voltmeter or a 12V test light? A haynes manual would be helpful so you can see the basic wiring circuits too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Rick 88||08-28-2001||05:57 PM||||If you car is a V6, a possible culprit is the ignition module inside the distributor. They tend to fail without notice. The car will crank but not start.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
